[{"code":"top_level_list_changed","severity":"error","span":{"file":"Main.beni","start":{"line":14,"col":17},"end":{"line":15,"col":97}},"title":"TOP-LEVEL LIST CHANGED","message":"`Dict.foldr` changes the dictionary `Main.shared` in place, and another use\nstill holds its storage.\n\n14|                Dict.foldr (Dict.fromList [ ( 1, 1 ), ( 2, 2 ) ]) shared λ_ x acc →\n                   ^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^ the storage is changed here\n6|shared = Dict.insert (Dict.empty ⊤) 1 [ 0 ]\n  ^^^^^^ the shared top-level collection is defined here\n\nChanging the slots or order would also change what the old dictionary observes.\n\nMake an explicit storage copy with `Dict.copy` before this write. Stored values\nremain shared; copy a stored value too if you need to change that value.\n\nTo keep the old storage unchanged, copy it at this use:\n\n14|                Dict.foldr (Dict.fromList [ ( 1, 1 ), ( 2, 2 ) ]) (Dict.copy shared) λ_ x acc →\n\nThis is sharing the code shows: Main.shared is a top-level value"},{"code":"top_level_list_changed","severity":"error","span":{"file":"Main.beni","start":{"line":14,"col":17},"end":{"line":15,"col":97}},"title":"TOP-LEVEL LIST CHANGED","message":"`Dict.foldr` changes `Main.shared[*]` in place, but it is `shared`, a top-level\nvalue.\n\n14|                Dict.foldr (Dict.fromList [ ( 1, 1 ), ( 2, 2 ) ]) shared λ_ x acc →\n                   ^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^ the list is changed in place here\n\n6|shared = Dict.insert (Dict.empty ⊤) 1 [ 0 ]\n  ^^^^^^ the top-level list is defined here\n\nA top-level value is shared by every part of the program and never changes:\nchanged in place, it would change for every part that reads it.\n\nMake `shared` a function that builds a fresh value at each call, or change a\ncopy: `List.copy shared[*]`.\n\nThis is the language's rule for top-level values, whether or not anything else\nreads the list (ownership-checker.md §4.2)."},{"code":"list_may_be_shared","severity":"error","span":{"file":"Main.beni","start":{"line":14,"col":17},"end":{"line":15,"col":97}},"title":"LIST MAY BE SHARED","message":"`Dict.foldr` changes `Main.shared[*]` in place, and the checker cannot show that\nnothing else still holds the list.\n\n14|                Dict.foldr (Dict.fromList [ ( 1, 1 ), ( 2, 2 ) ]) shared λ_ x acc →\n                   ^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^ the list is changed in place here\n\n6|shared = Dict.insert (Dict.empty ⊤) 1 [ 0 ]\n  ^^^^^^ the top-level list is defined here\n\nCopy the list with `List.copy` before it is changed, so the change cannot reach\nanything else that holds it.\n\nThis is a limit of the checker, not proof of sharing: Main.shared is a top-level\nvalue; the callee writes it only through an approximate step."},{"code":"list_may_be_shared","severity":"error","span":{"file":"Main.beni","start":{"line":14,"col":17},"end":{"line":15,"col":97}},"title":"LIST MAY BE SHARED","message":"`Dict.foldr` changes `Main.shared[*]` in place, and the checker cannot show that\nnothing else still holds the list.\n\n14|                Dict.foldr (Dict.fromList [ ( 1, 1 ), ( 2, 2 ) ]) shared λ_ x acc →\n                   ^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^ the list is changed in place here\n\n6|shared = Dict.insert (Dict.empty ⊤) 1 [ 0 ]\n  ^^^^^^ the top-level list is defined here\n\nCopy the list with `List.copy` before it is changed, so the change cannot reach\nanything else that holds it.\n\nThis is a limit of the checker, not proof of sharing: Main.shared is a top-level\nvalue; the callee writes it only through an approximate step."},{"code":"list_may_be_shared","severity":"error","span":{"file":"Main.beni","start":{"line":15,"col":21},"end":{"line":15,"col":97}},"title":"LIST MAY BE SHARED","message":"`Dict.update` changes the dictionary `acc` in place, and it needs the values\nstored in it not to share a list. They may.\n\n15|                    Dict.update acc 1 λold → Just (List.append (Maybe.withDefault old []) [ x ])\n                       ^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^ the values are changed here\n\nA storage copy with `Dict.copy` does not help: it is shallow, and the copy holds\nthe same values.\n\nGive each key a value of its own: where one list is stored a second time, store\n`List.copy` of it (or `Record.copy` of a record) instead.\n\nThis is a limit of the checker, not proof of sharing: it needs what Dict.foldr\nsupplies it not to share, and it may"},{"code":"list_may_be_shared","severity":"error","span":{"file":"Main.beni","start":{"line":15,"col":21},"end":{"line":15,"col":97}},"title":"LIST MAY BE SHARED","message":"`Dict.update` changes `acc[*]` in place, and the checker cannot show that\nnothing else still holds the list.\n\n15|                    Dict.update acc 1 λold → Just (List.append (Maybe.withDefault old []) [ x ])\n                       ^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^ the list is changed in place here\n\nCopy the list with `List.copy` before it is changed, so the change cannot reach\nanything else that holds it.\n\nThis is a limit of the checker, not proof of sharing: it needs what Dict.foldr\nsupplies it not to share, and it may."}]
